    "created_at": "2022-02-06T21:07:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-06T21:07:36Z",
    "body": "Yeah, the CSS Selectors spec is just wrong; it's unclear why they say that. They should fix it.\r\n\r\nThe current HTML spec (which governs how :target behaves, not the CSS spec) already says that `:target` should not change in reaction to pushState/replaceState, since they don't update the [target element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#target-element). So this issue can be closed.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like a new pseudo-class that matches the current fragment, and doesn't match the target element (which is only updated in specific conditions), I opened https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6942 where developers can advocate for that.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1030914480/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
