    "updated_at": "2023-04-11T05:37:46Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately [the workaround](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/639#issuecomment-285452237) isn't viable, since it triggers scroll to an anchored element upon navigation in Safari (works fine in Chrome, though). The whole reason of using `history.pushState()` instead of just assigning to the `location.hash` was to avoid page scrolling.\r\n\r\nAre there any methods to update the `:target` elements, but not scroll to them that work across browsers?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
